# Bundled broker ACL (copied by mosquitto-init next to the password file).
# Mosquitto 2.1 (plugins/acl-file): anything not granted to the user is
# refused (reads are checked on delivery, writes on publish).
#
# zigbee2mqtt: the bridge itself.
user zigbee2mqtt
topic readwrite zigbee2mqtt/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

# homeassistant: Home Assistant's MQTT integration, an allowlist (no
# zigbee2mqtt/# grant). Zigbee2MQTT 2.14 matches bridge requests
# case-insensitively (lib/extension/bridge.ts lowercases the key), so no
# denylist: whatever isn't listed is refused in every casing. Never
# granted: bridge requests other than permit_join (extensions / converters
# = code in the container, options, backup, restart, ...), bridge
# responses (the backup response holds the network key) and
# bridge/logging (Zigbee2MQTT logs every MQTT publish with its payload,
# lib/mqtt.ts, and forwards its log there).
user homeassistant
# MQTT discovery: Zigbee2MQTT's discovery configs; HA's birth message.
topic read homeassistant/#
topic write homeassistant/status
# Device and group state and availability (friendly names without "/";
# zigbee2mqtt/+ never matches a bridge topic, nothing is published at
# zigbee2mqtt/bridge itself).
topic read zigbee2mqtt/+
topic read zigbee2mqtt/+/availability
# Bridge status for Home Assistant's Zigbee2MQTT bridge entities.
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/state
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/info
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/devices
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/groups
topic read zigbee2mqtt/bridge/event
# Device and group commands: <name>/set|get[/<attribute>] and, with an
# endpoint, <name>/<endpoint>/set|get[/<attribute>] (Zigbee2MQTT's
# discovery command topics). None of these shapes is a bridge request
# Zigbee2MQTT acts on: no request key ends in set/get, and the extension /
# converter handlers need save|remove right after their name.
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/set
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/set/+
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/get
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/get/+
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/+/set
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/+/set/+
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/+/get
topic write zigbee2mqtt/+/+/get/+
# The one bridge request Home Assistant's Zigbee2MQTT entities may use
# (the "Permit join" switch).
topic write zigbee2mqtt/bridge/request/permit_join
